{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1494334228,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMDE1MjY0Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1504#issuecomment-300152646"},"message":"Ok, these are many issues in one.\n\n1) Not dumping the IncompleteResultsError -- easy, fine with me\n\n2) re grouping: difficult, anything that changes the order of things requires something more than result comes in, we act on it, done. we either want constant output, or we don't IMHO. Grouping in general would be easy -- I made the messages template plus values, so we can easily decide which ones are of the same kind.\n\n3) they rest I cannot comment on right now. for the first few hundred MBs and minutes it looked quite nice to me (mostly progress bars). I stopped it then.\n\n4) at present we render results (way more than before) AND we log (as much as before) -- I mentioned before that I think this should change, but got no super-threshold feedback on it yet.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1495121330,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMjQ0MDM2OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1504#issuecomment-302440368"},"message":"re groupping -- don't we pass up also results on failures?  then we could include error message in those (if not yet there), parse them (for get commands) to compile a list of remotes which need to be provided and output it at the end?  for error log messages -- we could  just swallow/filter out those specific ones whenever we expect them to possibly happen","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1495121412,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMjQ0MDc5NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1504#issuecomment-302440795"},"message":"I also wonder if default mode of reacting to errors should be 'continue' for get, drop, and install so a single run could be as complete as it could get?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1495194219,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMjY4MTM4MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1504#issuecomment-302681380"},"message":"Re 2.: \nI agree that is difficult in the sense of \"not flooding the screen\". But as an additional output at the end the way @yarikoptic proposed it (\"compile a list of remotes which need to be provided and output it at the end\") it's doable and may be useful.\n\nRe logging:\nI don't find the issue right now, but yes: @mih already pointed it out and proposed to at least change the log level (and the default level to actually print them out) at most layers. And I agree. I don't think swallowing them is a good approach though. We should have a consistent idea of what to log at what level and get away from the idea, that logging is some kind of default user output. Personally, I wouldn't even have a default level to print at all, but instead log to proper log files by default.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1495194838,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMjY4MzI0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1504#issuecomment-302683242"},"message":"I was planning to switch to `continue` as default error behavior for a while now.\n\nre logging: I am configuration the result status setting so that warnings are informative for the caller, this would be my preferred default log level.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1496833193,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTExMzQzNDkzMw=="},"status":2}]}